+# Feature Spec — STORY-015: Target Catalog ID + Listing-Status Read Sync
+
+**Phase path:** 1 → 6 → 7 → 8 → 11 → Done
+**Scope:** Small-Medium
+**Status:** Phase 6 complete
+**Depends on:** STORY-008 (items must exist; their product_status_ids are the poll targets)
+**Blocks:** Nothing
+
+---
+
+## 1. Problem
+
+GC's reporting layer tracks Target catalog state (`tcin`, `external_id`, `version`,
+`listing_status`, `validation_status`) but the columns are never populated after
+STORY-008 submits items. Operators cannot see "APPROVED / REJECTED / PENDING" status
+or validation errors without this read-back mirror.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Endpoint
+
+```
+GET /sellers/v1/sellers/{seller_id}/products/{product_id}/statuses/{product_status_id}
+```
+
+**Source:** `target-openapi.yaml` §getProductStatus (PDF p. 12–13, confidence: verified)
+
+Query parameter:
+- `expand=product_statuses` — returns full version history (all prior status records,
+  not just current). Default: current record only.
+
+---
+
+## 3. API Response Schema (`ProductStatus`)
+
+| Field | Type | Notes |
+|-------|------|-------|
+| `id` | string | product_status_id |
+| `listing_status` | enum | APPROVED, REJECTED, SUSPENDED, PENDING, UNLISTED |
+| `validation_status` | enum | INITIATED (only documented value; others possible) |
+| `version` | integer | increments on each update |
+| `current` | boolean | true = latest version |
+| `errors` | array | ProductStatusError records; JSON-serialized in DB |
+| `created` | datetime | ISO 8601 |
+| `last_modified` | datetime | ISO 8601 |
+
+**Note:** `tcin` and `external_id` are NOT returned in the `ProductStatus` body.
+They must be supplied by the caller from the product registry (STORY-008 write-path
+stores these at creation time).
+
+---
+
+## 4. Mapping: `ProductStatus` → `TargetCatalogStatus` (DB model)
+
+| DB Column | Source | rep.dim_sku analog | Notes |
+|-----------|--------|--------------------|-------|
+| `tcin` | caller-supplied (product registry) | `tcin` | Target Catalog Item Number |
+| `external_id` | caller-supplied (product registry) | `external_id` | Seller SKU |
+| `product_status_id` | `ProductStatus.id` | — | PK from Target |
+| `version` | `ProductStatus.version` | `version` | increments per update |
+| `is_current` | `ProductStatus.current` | — | true = latest |
+| `listing_status` | `ProductStatus.listing_status` | `listing_status` | stored as-is |
+| `validation_status` | `ProductStatus.validation_status` | `validation_status` | stored as-is if known |
+| `validation_status_raw` | `ProductStatus.validation_status` | — | always stored; allows unknown values |
+| `errors_json` | `ProductStatus.errors` | — | JSON text of error array |
+| `status_created_at` | `ProductStatus.created` | — | |
+| `status_last_modified_at` | `ProductStatus.last_modified` | — | |
+| `synced_at` | server-set UTC timestamp | — | |
+
+**Unknown `validation_status` handling:** If `validation_status` is not in the known
+enum (`INITIATED`), store the raw value in `validation_status_raw` and set
+`validation_status = None`. Log a warning. Ingest must NOT crash.
+
+---
+
+## 5. DB Migration
+
+Migration file: `alembic/versions/002_catalog_sync_status.py`
+
+Table: `target_catalog_status`
+
+```sql
+CREATE TABLE target_catalog_status (
+    id                      SERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
+    tcin                    TEXT NOT NULL,
+    external_id             TEXT NOT NULL,
+    product_status_id       TEXT NOT NULL,
+    version                 INTEGER,
+    is_current              BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE,
+    listing_status          TEXT,
+    validation_status       TEXT,
+    validation_status_raw   TEXT,
+    errors_json             TEXT,
+    status_created_at       TIMESTAMPTZ,
+    status_last_modified_at TIMESTAMPTZ,
+    synced_at               TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),
+    UNIQUE (tcin, product_status_id)
+);
+```
+
+Index on `(tcin, is_current)` for the common reporting query pattern.
+
+---
+
+## 6. Polling Design
+
+### sync_once — single poll cycle
+
+```
+sync_once(client, items, seller_id, session)
+  items: list of {"tcin": str, "external_id": str, "product_status_id": str}
+  For each item:
+    raw = client.get_product_status(seller_id, tcin, product_status_id)
+    row = map_product_status(raw, tcin, external_id)
+    upsert row into target_catalog_status ON CONFLICT (tcin, product_status_id) DO UPDATE
+```
+
+### expand variant — full version history
+
+```
+sync_once(..., expand=True)
+  Passes expand=product_statuses; response includes all version history.
+  Each version record upserted individually.
+```
+
+### Polling cadence
+
+- **Default:** hourly cron (pending scheduler story)
+- **Trigger-based:** hook into STORY-008 post-submit event (future)
+- **CLI:** `python -m app.catalog_sync.cli sync-once [--product-id TCIN] [--expand]`
+
+---
+
+## 7. Dependency Injection
+
+`TargetCatalogReadClient` accepts:
+- `base_url: str = "https://api.target.com"`
+- `auth_token: str = ""`
+
+Test/local environments use `AsyncMock(spec=TargetCatalogReadClient)`. No real HTTP
+calls during tests.
+
+---
+
+## 8. Open Questions
+
+| OQ | Question | Impact |
+|----|----------|--------|
+| OQ-1 | Is `product_id` in the URL the `tcin` or the seller's `external_id`? PDF p.12 uses `product_id` without defining it. | Affects how we construct the client call. Design assumes `tcin` = `product_id`. |
+| OQ-2 | What `validation_status` values beyond `INITIATED` exist in practice? | Unknown values handled via `validation_status_raw` fallback. |
+| OQ-3 | Does `expand=product_statuses` return a list or nest within the single object? | Test fixture uses list. Phase 8 to verify shape from staging. |
+| OQ-4 | How many `product_status_ids` does a single product accumulate over time? | Affects polling scope. Phase 8 cap at 100 per product (tunable). |
+
+---
+
+## 9. Acceptance Criteria (carried from seed)
+
+| SC | Description |
+|----|-------------|
+| SC-1 | Catalog status sync works against staging |
+| SC-2 | Mapping to `rep.dim_sku` populated; columns equivalent to Amazon catalog dim |
+| SC-3 | Unknown enum values (`validation_status`) handled gracefully |
